From: PS3 Custom Toolchain
Subject: [PATCH] rs6000: ext-dce off by default for powerpc64-ps3-elf ILP32

Under the PS3 ILP32 model pointers are 32 bits, held zero-extended in
64-bit registers (Pmode DImode, POINTERS_EXTEND_UNSIGNED), and the PPU
forms 64-bit effective addresses from all 64 bits.  With GCC 16, zlib's
adler32 at -O2 looped forever on any input of 33 bytes: ext-dce turned
(zero_extend:DI (reg:SI)) of the post-loop buffer pointer -- a 32-bit
value that had wrapped, formed by final value replacement -- into a
paradoxical subreg, and combine then folded the address arithmetic into
a 64-bit subtraction, so the address kept a set upper half.  The
extension survives every pass up to ext-dce and is gone after combine;
-fno-ext-dce alone restores correct code.

As containment, keep ext-dce off by default under ILP32 (in
rs6000_override_options_after_change, so optimize attributes and pragmas
get the same default).  An explicit -fext-dce is honoured and is known to
be unsafe for this shape; -fno-ext-dce is honoured.  LP64 is unchanged.
Whether ext-dce or an earlier RTL expression is at fault is still being
established.

diff --git a/gcc/config/rs6000/rs6000.cc b/gcc/config/rs6000/rs6000.cc
index 49a6cb3..678d620 100644
--- a/gcc/config/rs6000/rs6000.cc
+++ b/gcc/config/rs6000/rs6000.cc
@@ -3438,6 +3438,20 @@ rs6000_override_options_after_change (void)
      until the define_insn_and_splits are fixed.  */
   if (!OPTION_SET_P (flag_late_combine_instructions))
     flag_late_combine_instructions = 0;
+
+#ifdef POWERPC_CELL64LV2
+  /* PS3 LV2 ILP32: pointers are 32 bits, held zero-extended in 64-bit
+     registers, and the PPU forms 64-bit effective addresses from all 64
+     bits.  ext-dce has been seen to turn the zero-extension of a 32-bit
+     pointer value that wrapped (a post-loop pointer formed by final value
+     replacement) into a paradoxical subreg, after which combine folded the
+     address arithmetic into 64 bits and the address kept a set upper half
+     (zlib's adler32 looped).  Keep the pass off by default under ILP32;
+     an explicit -fext-dce is honoured, and is known unsafe for that
+     shape.  LP64 is unchanged.  */
+  if (!TARGET_LP64 && !OPTION_SET_P (flag_ext_dce))
+    flag_ext_dce = 0;
+#endif
 }
 
 #ifdef TARGET_USES_LINUX64_OPT
